[h2]Polaris interface update[/h2]
Clearer controls across all six tabs, full warning details and an installed weapon-group picker. Switched-off weapons stay visible with an explanation. Confirm group handoffs explicitly: the old group may resume native automatic fire; the new group stays held. Left-click Volleys to increase, right-click to decrease; both wrap from 1 to 9. Existing automatic missile restrictions remain in place.
Browser checks do not establish Unity interaction approval. The recent refresh pacing remains in place; further performance recordings are deferred.

[h2]Polaris readability correction[/h2]
Dark button faces now keep labels readable in every interaction state. This fixes the white-button regression reported in game. The corrected native appearance still awaits owner playtesting.
Separate live frames, smaller command/help text and compact buttons keep controls within their sections. Departure, Info and dialogs scroll inside inset areas; Resume, Disengage and Cease Fire stay fixed below them.

[b]Secured towing[/b]
Approach, Rendezvous, Follow, FCS and Combat support one securely braced tow in free space, using native RCS/torch controls and clearance for both hulls. Engage still grants firing permission separately; an attached ship cannot be selected as the fire target. Brace faults cancel aiming and firing without automatic restart. Release the tow before Dock, Approach & Dock or industrial close work. Stations, mooring, towing chains and unsecured attachments remain blocked. Live towing handling awaits owner testing.

[b]Item handling correction[/b]
Keep board and remnant pickup/drop actions consistent with their actual stack limits through the shared handling helper. Preserve module slots, repair, restore, dismantling and navigation behaviour. Requires Phobos Framework 0.30.2. Live menu and inventory handling remain owner-tested.

[b]Merchant and salvage update[/b]
Raise equipment offer chances to at least 85% before the availability setting, fill missing N1/N2/N3 offers at general suppliers, and include all three boards in native module salvage. New configurations default to 30% total per eligible roll; existing saved settings remain authoritative. One board per successful salvage choice, with damaged-only pools preserved. Normal restocking and new loot generation are required; existing inventories stay as they are. Offline checks are not gameplay validation.

[b]Item-action audit[/b]
The complete item-action audit covers all boards and residues. Boards fit native module slots rather than floor INSTALL; offline maintenance registration checks do not establish live menu approval.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/item-handling-audit.md]Complete findings and item ledger[/url]

